
# Board identity for this repo's agent — and ONLY the identity.
#
# Deliberately absent: any store location or backend. An explicit pin WINS the
# resolution chain, so pinning is not a safety net here, it is the failure
# mode. This file has now hit that twice:
#
#   SCITEX_TODO_TASKS_YAML_SHARED="$HOME/.scitex/todo/tasks.yaml"   (removed in #59)
#   SCITEX_CARDS_DB + SCITEX_CARDS_STORE_BACKEND, naming a local file
#   and the retired engine that read it                             (removed in #68)
#
# Both named a store that does not exist. The second pair was added while
# fixing the first, which is the part worth remembering: correcting the
# variable's NAME while keeping a hand-written local path just re-pointed the
# same gun. The board has been PostgreSQL since the cutover; the comment that
# used to sit here still described it as a local file.
#
# What the removal actually buys is a LOUD failure instead of a quiet wrong
# answer. Measured both ways:
#
#   with the pin      -> a local file under ~/.scitex/cards/, opened happily
#   without the pin   -> StoreUnavailableError            (refuses to guess)
#
# The pinned form is the dangerous one precisely because it succeeds. An
# unreachable store presents as "the board is empty", never as an error, so
# anyone working in this repo files cards the fleet never sees. That exact
# shape caused an hours-long silent MCP write outage in scitex-cards on
# 2026-07-19.
#
# The working DSN is injected by the environment that runs the agent, which is
# the single place it should live. Every other repo in the fleet sets identity
# alone; this one now matches.
#
# The legacy SCITEX_TODO_* aliases are NOT written by hand:
# scitex_cards._env_compat.mirror_env copies every SCITEX_CARDS_* key into its
# SCITEX_TODO_* twin at import. Writing both would add a second place for the
# pair to disagree, and a store whose two names resolve differently is exactly
# what took the live board down.
export SCITEX_CARDS_AGENT_ID="scitex-tunnel"
